  "notes": "USAGE:\n{軽|かろ}んじる is a literary and formal verb. In everyday speech, {軽|かる}く{見|み}る or ばかにする are more common. It appears frequently in written commentary, editorials, and formal discourse.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nKami-ichidan (ru-verb). Transitive. The older form {軽|かろ}んずる also exists but is archaic.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {命|いのち}を{軽|かろ}んじる (to make light of life)\n- {人権|じんけん}を{軽|かろ}んじる (to disregard human rights)\n- {伝統|でんとう}を{軽|かろ}んじる (to belittle tradition)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {侮|あなど}る: to look down on, to scorn\n- {見下|みくだ}す: to look down on (more colloquial)\n- {蔑|さげす}む: to despise, to hold in contempt",
